                             Last Release!
                             ÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ

     Well, the time has come for me to give up on XHost. It was an
     interesting project for quite a few years, but now I'm onto more
     challenging pursuits. As far as I could tell, interest in XHost was
     minimal at best, so there isn't too much pressure on me to develop
     new material. In another way, I think that an infusion of source
     code will help out a lot of people playing the power of SALT.
     I also got a few requests to customize the prompts, and this is the
     easiest way to deal with that :). Finally, I am not up to the task
     of writing a new version for TFW. It would be really neat if
     somebody did build on XHost to accomplish that, and I hope they
     will continue to respect the freeware spirit of the software.

     Most of the code is reasonably well documented. Some areas
     (especially in the full-screen editor) are a challenge even for me
     after a while. I do not claim to follow the most wonderful
     programming habits, so variable names aren't always meaningful,
     etc. The file PLAN contains most of the structures and file
     formats that I used, although it is possible that there are
     discrepancies with reality. Anyway, it's all in your hands now!

     I have basically included the whole of my script directory. There
     are some scripts which contain ideas I toyed with, so they may also
     provide some help to those who want to take advantage of Telix's
     strength. I will very gladly help anybody who has problems
     understanding the code, but I'm not a SALT tutor, so make sure that
     you have a handle on the basics before you give me a yell.

     Most of the large scripts need to be compiled with a 2048 byte
     stack. I usually relied on the COS batch file, which allowed me to
     assign a one-letter key to each script. It would then take care of
     stack sizes for me.


                         Notes on Installation
                         ÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ

     Installation is still manual. It is recommended that you create an
     XHOST directory for the data files.

     All files with an SLC extension must be placed inside your script
     directory (defined in Telix, Alt-O F C), and all other files must
     be copied to your XHost data directory (defined in XHost Setup,
     System, XHost directory).

     The following files are in the distribution archive:

     Misceallaneous files:

     FILE_ID.DIZ    XHost's description
     README.1ST     This file
     QDMENU.ZIP     This contains a MENU.DEF and MENU001.ASC for a
                    simple setup.
     XHvvv.NEW      Changes and bug fixes in this version


     In script directory:

     ADD.SLC        Adds files to FILES.LST in current directory
     DOOR.SLC       Information file converter for doors
     EDIT.SLC       User Editor
     EDITOR.SLC     Message Editor
     GENP.SLC       Generates rejection path list for Bimodem
     SETUP.SLC      Setup script
     SORT.SLC       Sorts FILES.LST in all directories
     XHOST.SLC      Main host script
     XHOST.DOC      Docs

     In Telix directory:

     PACK.EXE       Data file packer

     In XHost data directory:

     ARCS.CFG       Archiver configuration file
     BIMOD.ASC      Bimodem help file
     MENU.DEF       Menu definition file
     MENU000.ASC    Sysop menu
     MENU000.ANS
     MENU001.ASC    Main menu
     MENU001.ANS
     MENU002.ASC    File menu
     MENU002.ANS
     MENU003.ASC    Archive viewing menu
     MENU003.ANS
     MENU004.ANS    User setup menu
     MENU004.ASC
     PROTO.ASC      Protocol table


                                Support
                                ÄÄÄÄÄÄÄ


     Well, you're more or less on your own now. XHost is relatively
     stable, so most people shouldn't have trouble with it. And
     hopefully most glitches should be easy to fix by wading through the
     code.

